this section gives you an introduction  to cloud cloud computing enables you to  consume server infrastructure and  software platforms as a service over the  Internet  you don't have to buy and maintain  expensive Hardware in your data center  infrastructure includes raw resources  such as virtual machines networking  storage and more these resources are the  fundamental building blocks of cloud  computing when you consume  infrastructure as a service I as you  have greater control over the resources  but also greater management overhead for  example consider a virtual machine you  need to install upgrade and patch all  the software required to run your  application you can configure your  virtual machines to scale based on the  load on your application Google compute  engine networking and load balancers are  examples of I as platform as-a-service  paas provides a platform with managed  services where runtime environment and  network settings are pre-configured this  makes it easier for you to develop and  deploy your application Google App  Engine is an example of platform  as-a-service  Google App Engine comes pre-configured  with runtimes for Java Python node and  more software upgrades and patches are  automatically applied load balancing is  also pre-configured this enables the  developer to focus on the application  logic only instead of worrying about  infrastructure setup with software  as-a-service  SAS entire applications are managed and  made available in the cloud environment  Gmail is an example of a software as a  service this slide shows how you can use  Google cloud platform for application  data application logic and integration  with other Google services imagine an  online shopping website or a mobile app  the application needs to store and  retrieve different types of data as  follows the website or app displays  images of items such as shoes and  clothes these images can be stored in  Google Cloud storage high volume semi  structured data like gaming or streaming  data can be stored in no sequel  databases such as cloud datastore and  BigTable customer information can be  stored in a relational database such as  cloud sequel or cloud spanner  application logic can be deployed and  executed  on Google App Engine or google  kubernetes engine you can integrate with  other Google services such as Google  Maps and YouTube all of this  infrastructure can be started up in just  a few minutes without buying hardware or  installing software
 

